{"text": "Trends toward a marked increase in competition have forced companies to adopt much more aggressive innovation strategies. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Innovation provides one way of getting out of the competition, which is to say situations in which activities are not very profitable. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Innovation indeed provides an opportunity to set oneself apart and temporarily to assume a monopoly position, this provides an opportunity to make a profit either by increasing prices or by reducing costs. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> There are, of course, other means that can be relied upon to survive and prosper in a market economy. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> These conventional means rely mainly on geographical distances and transportation costs, the limited capacity of consumers to compare prices and qualities fully, and the existence of regulated activities. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> All these mechanisms reduce the degree of competition and allow companies to survive even if they do not have the best product or the cheapest price. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> However, globalization, deregulation, and some antitrust policies are all trends which dramatically weaken the effectiveness of those conventional means. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Innovative strategies, therefore, appear as the only way to survive and prosper in the new competitive environment.", "alignment": {"characters": ["T", "r", "e", "n", "d", "s", " ", "t", "o", "w", "a", "r", "d", " ", "a", " ", "m", "a", "r", "k", "e", "d", " ", "i", "n", "c", "r", "e", "a", "s", "e", " ", "i", "n", " ", "c", "o", "m", "p", "e", "t", "i", "t", "i", "o", "n", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "f", "o", "r", "c", "e", "d", " ", "c", "o", "m", "p", "a", "n", "i", "e", "s", " ", "t", "o", " ", "a", "d", "o", "p", "t", " ", "m", "u", "c", "h", " ", "m", "o", "r", "e", " ", "a", "g", "g", "r", "e", "s", "s", "i", "v", "e", " ", "i", "n", "n", "o", "v", "a", "t", "i", "o", "n", " ", "s", "t", "r", "a", "t", "e", "g", "i", "e", "s", "